| NumPy | Numerical operations |
| OpenCV | Image preprocessing |
| Streamlit | Web application |
| Streamlit Drawable Canvas | Drawing interface |

## 🏗️ CNN Model Architecture

The CNN extracts visual features from handwritten images and classifies them into 10 digit categories.

```text
Input Image (28 × 28 × 1)
          |
          v
Conv2D (32 filters, 3 × 3, ReLU)
          |
          v
Max Pooling (2 × 2)
          |
          v
Conv2D (64 filters, 3 × 3, ReLU)
          |
          v
Max Pooling (2 × 2)
          |
          v
Flatten Layer
          |
          v
Dense (128 neurons, ReLU)
          |
          v
Output (10 neurons, Softmax)
          |
          v
Predicted Digit (0–9)
```

### Layer Details

| Layer | Configuration | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Input | 28 × 28 × 1 | Accepts grayscale images |
| Conv2D | 32 filters, 3 × 3 | Extracts basic features |
| MaxPooling2D | 2 × 2 | Reduces dimensions |
| Conv2D | 64 filters, 3 × 3 | Learns deeper features |
| MaxPooling2D | 2 × 2 | Further reduces dimensions |
| Flatten | — | Converts feature maps into a vector |
| Dense | 128 neurons, ReLU | Learns classification patterns |
| Output | 10 neurons, Softmax | Predicts digits 0–9 |

### ⚙️ Training Configuration

- **Optimizer:** Adam
- **Loss Function:** Sparse Categorical Crossentropy
- **Evaluation Metric:** Accuracy
- **Epochs:** 5
- **Batch Size:** 64
- **Validation Split:** 10%

The Softmax output generates probabilities for all 10 digit classes. The class with the highest probability becomes the final prediction.

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
handwritten-digit-recognition/
│
├── app.py
├── digit_recognition_model.keras
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

## 💻 Run Locally

**1. Clone the repository**

```bash
git clone https://github.com/loki25590/handwritten-digit-recognition.git
cd handwritten-digit-recognition
```

**2. Install dependencies**

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

**3. Run the application**

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

